A||N||8||burdell1||Car Accident + Power mirror woes||||1||
Z||000000||burdell1||05-11-2000||08:47 AM||||I recently got into a car accident. Luckily the only thing that was damaaged was my power mirror fell off and is hanging by the cord (it still works!) It looks like it is just missing screws or something. Is that something that can be ordered through GM?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-11-2000||09:19 AM||||I'm pretty sure that the "bolts" are an integral part of the mirror, but I could be wrong.  If you need another set of mirrors, LMK.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-11-2000||10:31 AM||||Take off the interior door skin and recover the original stud for the mirror. They should be laying in the bottom of the door someplace.<P>You can epoxy the studs back into the mirror's holes or whatever. the just put the mirror back on the door.<P>Unplug the mirror or tie it up or something to protect the cord untill you replace the studs.||||reg||1
Z||000003||burdell1||05-15-2000||01:59 PM||||I can't find the studs.....Does anyone out there know where you can buy some? or does anyone have any for sale?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-15-2000||04:05 PM||||Just go to the hardware/carparts store and get 2 studs or some threaded rod about the right size, doesn't have to be an exact match. the length doesn't matter as long as they reach thru the door enough to get nuts on. (You'll have to cut the rod to length anyway if you go that route.)<P>Tip, when cutting rod, put a couple nuts on the rod before cutting. thread them down to each side of where you're cutting, leave plenty of room to saw. then after you cut the nut will help clean up the threads as you thread them off over the new cut ends.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||05-15-2000||10:50 PM||||You could call Kick Hill Farms or Twin Lake Fiero or the Fiero Factory and get a complete salvaged mirror assembly.  May be better than trying to jerry rig a repair.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||05-16-2000||11:18 AM||||if the shell has any other damage that's a good option. He seems to indicate the shell is fine except it lacks studs now. studs are cheap to fix, and done right will be as strong or stronger. It's not a high precision item to begin with.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Racer 1||05-16-2000||10:22 PM||||Just use some ducktape to patch that mirror on.||||reg||3
Z||000008||theogre||05-17-2000||09:39 AM||||Hey, This ain't the red green show.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
